{"step_index":2077,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T03:02:52Z","thinking":"**Constructing The Harness**\n\nI'm now generating `ops/runtime/atomic_cacheline_race_fuzzer.c` using `write_to_file`. The harness will test false-sharing and cache line bouncing. Specifically, it involves 10 threads concurrently hammering 10 adjacent 64-bit variables within a single 64-byte cache line to isolate the effect.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"/*\\n * XORAS HARDWARE CONCURRENCY & CACHE-LINE RACE FUZZER\\n * Target: Expose 64-byte cache line contention, false-sharing latency penalties,\\n *         and non-atomic state tearing across Apple Silicon M4 10 CPU cores.\\n */\\n\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <stdbool.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <unistd.h>\\n#include <pthread.h>\\n#include <stdatomic.h>\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n#include <mach/mach_time.h>\\n\\n#define NUM_CORES 10\\n#define ITERATIONS 5000000\\n\\nstatic double get_time_ms(void) {\\n    static mach_timebase_info_data_t timebase;\\n    if (timebase.denom == 0) {\\n        mach_timebase_info(&timebase);\\n    }\\n    uint64_t time = mach_absolute_time();\\n    return (double)time * timebase.numer / timebase.denom / 1e6;\\n}\\n\\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// TEST 1: UNPADDED CACHE LINE FALSE SHARING (10 CORES CONTESTING 1 CACHE LINE)\\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\ntypedef struct {\\n    uint64_t counter[NUM_CORES]; // Unpadded: all 10 counters fit in ONE 64-byte cache line!\\n} UnpaddedCacheLine;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    struct {\\n        uint64_t counter;\\n        uint8_t padding[120]; // Padded: Each counter gets its own isolated 128-byte cache line!\\n    } slots[NUM_CORES];\\n} PaddedCacheLine;\\n\\nstatic UnpaddedCacheLine unpadded_target;\\nstatic PaddedCacheLine padded_target;\\n\\nstatic void *unpadded_worker(void *arg) {\\n    int id = (int)(intptr_t)arg;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < ITERATIONS; i++) {\\n        unpadded_target.counter[id]++; // Causes massive cache line invalidation ping-pong!\\n    }\\n    return NULL;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void *padded_worker(void *arg) {\\n    int id = (int)(intptr_t)arg;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < ITERATIONS; i++) {\\n        padded_target.slots[id].counter++; // Clean L1 cache line isolation!\\n    }\\n    return NULL;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void benchmark_cache_line_contention(void) {\\n    printf(\\\"\\\\n🔥 EXPERIMENT 1: 10-CORE CACHE-LINE FALSE SHARING BENCHMARK\\\\n\\\");\\\n<truncated 4658 bytes>","Description":"\"Create cache line contention and 128-bit state tearing race fuzzer\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/runtime/atomic_cacheline_race_fuzzer.c\"","toolAction":"\"Creating C cacheline race fuzzer\"","toolSummary":"\"Creating atomic race fuzzer\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
